   "when": "2026-11-23 16:56",
   "sent": "positive",
   "txt": "**1. Single Most Important Fact**  \nICRA reaffirmed Titan Company's top-tier credit ratings ([ICRA]AAA (Stable) / [ICRA]A1+) across all rated debt programs and assigned ratings to an enhanced working capital facility increased by Rs. 2,000 crore (from Rs. 14,750 crore to Rs. 16,750 crore).\n\n---\n\n**2. Key Numbers Exactly as Stated**  \n*No financial performance metrics (Revenue, EBITDA, PAT) were disclosed in this filing.*  \n\n* **Fixed Deposit Programme (Long-term):** Rs. 3,000 crore | `[ICRA]AAA (Stable)` (reaffirmed)  \n* **Working Capital Facilities (Long-term / Short-term, Fund/Non-fund based):** Rs. 16,750 crore (increased from Rs. 14,750 crore) | `[ICRA]AAA (Stable) / [ICRA]A1+` (reaffirmed and assigned for enhanced amount)  \n* **Term Loans (Long-term Fund-based):** Rs. 1,000 crore | `[ICRA]AAA (Stable)` (reaffirmed)  \n* **Total Rated Amount:** Rs. 20,750.00 crore  \n\n---\n\n**3. Management Guidance & Forward Statements**  \nNone provided in the document.\n\n---\n\n**4. What a Shareholder Should Watch or Act On**  \nNo action required. Shareholders can note the reaffirmation of the highest credit profile and monitor the deployment of the additional Rs. 2,000 crore in working capital facilities to support inventory and business growth.\n\n---\n\n**5. One-Line Net Read**  \n**Neutral to mildly positive:** Routine reaffirmation of the highest credit rating (`AAA`), with expanded working capital headroom to support ongoing operational requirements."
  },
